## Customization not working?

If apply/`new project` still shows defaults (e.g. only `my-project`) or files look unchanged:

1. **Variables without EJS do not rewrite files.** A `[variables.*]` entry with no matching `.taito/**/*.ejs` only affects `.taito/project.meta.toml` and future defaults. Fix: add the EJS mirror → `taito build` → re-test.
2. **`--json`, `-c`, `cat`, `write`, and `finalize` never prompt.** They use config defaults and/or the answers file. With bare `--json` you will always see defaults.
3. **Components are not EJS locals.** `<% if (docs) %>` fails if `docs` is only a `[components.*]` key. Use a boolean **variable** for section toggles inside a file; use a **component** to omit whole path trees / skills.
4. **Smoke test after edits:**

```bash
# answers.toml — real values, not just defaults
PROJECT_NAME = "acme"
USE_TYPESCRIPT = true

[components]
architecture_docs = true

taito build   # in the template directory
taito apply cat -t <template> -c answers.toml --file AGENT.md
```

Runtime contract (prompts, merge, apply vs new): [references/RUNTIME.md](references/RUNTIME.md).

### Prompt vs defaults

| Command | Prompts? |
|---------|----------|
| `taito new project` (no `-c`) | **yes** |
| `taito apply plan` (no `--json`, no `-c`) | **yes** |
| `apply … --json`, `-c`, `cat` / `write` / `finalize` | **no** — defaults or answers file |

When using `--json` as an agent: **ask the user**, write `answers.toml`, pass `-c`. Follow **apply-template** for the full apply workflow — do not treat bare `--json` / `finalize` as sufficient customization.

## Authoring checklist

Copy-paste when finishing a template:

- [ ] Every user-facing string that should vary has a `[variables.*]` **and** a matching `.taito/**/*.ejs`
- [ ] Every optional tree or skill package has a `[components.*]` with `paths` / `skills`
- [ ] Section toggles inside a file → boolean **variables**; whole directories/skills → **components**
- [ ] EJS uses only variable names as locals — never component names
- [ ] After edits: `taito build` in the template directory
- [ ] Smoke: `answers.toml` + `taito apply cat -t <name> -c answers.toml --file <path>` for each templated file
- [ ] Registered: `taito add <path>` then `taito list`

## Quick Reference

```bash
# Register a local template (must be a git repo with template.config.toml)
taito add ~/Work/project-template

# Register from GitHub (cloned into ~/.taito/templates/<name>)
taito add owner/repo

# Duplicate → fresh git history at a new path
taito add ~/Work/my-variant --duplicate project-template

# Extend → git worktree + branch of the base
taito add ~/Work/my-child --extend project-template

# Initialize a project (path defaults to .; prompts unless -c)
taito new project -t project-template
taito new project ./acme-app -t project-template
taito new project -t project-template -c answers.toml

# Pull template updates into a project or child template
taito update

# Apply onto an existing project — use apply-template skill.
# Agents: collect answers first; --json never prompts.
taito apply plan -t project-template -c answers.toml --json
taito apply cat -t project-template -c answers.toml --file AGENT.md
taito apply finalize -t project-template -c answers.toml

# List / remove
taito list
taito remove project-template
```

Preferred agent for examples: **<%= PREFERRED_AGENT %>**.

## Template structure

```
my-template/                    # must be a git repository
├── .taito/
│   ├── template.config.toml    # required
│   ├── AGENT.md.ejs            # optional customization points
│   └── docs/PROJECT.md.ejs
├── AGENT.md                    # defaults / non-templated files
├── docs/
├── .agents/skills/...          # skills may be customizable
└── .git/
```

See [references/TEMPLATE-FORMAT.md](references/TEMPLATE-FORMAT.md) for the config schema, components, and EJS rules.

## Skills inside templates

- **Customizable skills** (`.taito/skill.config.toml`) are **not** rendered by the template engine. During `taito new project`, taito runs the normal skill customizer for each included customizable skill.
- **Standard skills** are copied with the project tree like any other files.
- Use `[components.*.skills]` to gate optional skill packages.

## Duplicate vs extend

| | Duplicate | Extend |
|---|-----------|--------|
| Git | Fresh `git init` | Worktree + branch `taito/<name>` of the base repo |
| Updates | Independent | `taito update` merges base into the child |
| Use when | Fork you will diverge heavily | Variant that should keep receiving base changes |

Details: [references/EXTEND-AND-DUPLICATE.md](references/EXTEND-AND-DUPLICATE.md).

## Updates

- **Projects** store origin in `.taito/project.meta.toml`. `taito update` re-renders the template at the old and new commits and three-way-merges into the project (git `merge-file`), so local edits are preserved when possible.
- **Child templates** run a git merge from the base tip.

See [references/UPDATE.md](references/UPDATE.md) and [references/RUNTIME.md](references/RUNTIME.md).

